        "original_id": "55052e8c-9523-550e-8109-2bfa64050ba9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: André Jardin, Alexis de Tocqueville, Lydia Davis, Robert Hemenway\n- Roles: biographer, historian, translator, author\n- Works: Tocqueville: A Biography, Democracy in America, De La Démocratie en Amérique\n- Topics: 19th century French history\n\nFacts:\n- André Jardin was born in 1912 and died in 1996.\n- André Jardin was a French biographer and historian.\n- André Jardin was best known for his studies of Alexis de Tocqueville and 19th century French history.\n- Alexis de Tocqueville was the author of Democracy in America, also titled De La Démocratie en Amérique.\n- Democracy in America was a classic French text published in two volumes.\n- André Jardin's studies were translated into English as Tocqueville: A Biography in 1988.\n- Lydia Davis and Robert Hemenway translated Tocqueville: A Biography into English.\n- Tocqueville: A Biography was acclaimed as the definitive account of the life and career of Alexis de Tocqueville.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
