        "original_id": "13479bfc-f366-5ab6-97c5-d5c0430c0bb3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: André Jardin, Alexis de Tocqueville, Lydia Davis, Robert Hemenway\n- Works: Alexis de Tocqueville: 1805-1859, Tocqueville: A Biography, Democracy in America, De La Démocratie en Amérique\n- Topics: Biography, Translation, Publication\n\nFacts:\n- In 1835, Alexis de Tocqueville published the first volume of De La Démocratie en Amérique.\n- In 1840, Alexis de Tocqueville published the second volume of De La Démocratie en Amérique.\n- De La Démocratie en Amérique is a classic French text by Alexis de Tocqueville.\n- In 1984, André Jardin published the biography Alexis de Tocqueville: 1805-1859.\n- In 1988, Lydia Davis and Robert Hemenway translated Alexis de Tocqueville: 1805-1859 into English as Tocqueville: A Biography.\n- André Jardin's Alexis de Tocqueville: 1805-1859 was acclaimed as the definitive account of the life and career of Alexis de Tocqueville, the author of Democracy in America.",
